{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"0458958dff13f044","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph Phase1_Metadata_Extraction_and_Relationship_Discovery [\"Phase 1: Metadata Extraction & Relationship Discovery\"]\n        A[Load All Sources] --> B[Build Relationship Graph]\n        B --> C[Create Global Context Document]\n        \n        B --> D[Extract Foreign Keys]\n        B --> E[Identify Naming Patterns]\n        B --> F[Map Business Entities]\n        \n        D --> G[Relationship Index]\n        E --> G\n        F --> G\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Phase2_Hierarchical_Rule_Generation [\"Phase 2: Hierarchical Rule Generation\"]\n        subgraph Column_Level_Processing [\"Column Level Processing\"]\n            H[Select Source] --> I[Load Tables for Source]\n            I --> J[Load Columns for Each Table]\n            J --> K[Create Column Batches\\n10-15 columns each]\n            \n            K --> L[Prepare Column Context]\n            L --> L1[Column Metadata]\n            L --> L2[Parent Table Context]\n            L --> L3[Source Identity]\n            L --> L4[Relationship Context]\n            L --> L5[Sample Values]\n            \n            L1 & L2 & L3 & L4 & L5 --> M[LLM Call: Column Rules]\n            M --> N[Column Validation Rules]\n        end\n        \n        subgraph Table_Level_Processing [\"Table Level Processing\"]\n            I --> O[Process Each Table]\n            O --> P[Prepare Table Context]\n            \n            P --> P1[Table Metadata]\n            P --> P2[All Column Names]\n            P --> P3[Primary Keys]\n            P --> P4[Foreign Key Relationships]\n            P --> P5[Referenced By Tables]\n            \n            P1 & P2 & P3 & P4 & P5 --> Q[LLM Call: Table Rules]\n            Q --> R[Table Validation Rules]\n        end\n        \n        subgraph Source_Level_Processing [\"Source Level Processing\"]\n            H --> S[Prepare Source Context]\n            S --> S1[Source Metadata]\n            S --> S2[Table Inventory]\n            S --> S3[Aggregated Relationships]\n            S --> S4[Business Context]\n            \n            S1 & S2 & S3 & S4 --> T[LLM Call: Source Rules]\n            T --> U[Source Validation Rules]\n        end\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Phase3_Cross_Entity_Validation [\"Phase 3: Cross-Entity Validation\"]\n        subgraph Inter_Table_Rules [\"Inter-Table Rules\"]\n            V[Group Related Tables\\n3-5 tables per group] --> W[Prepare Relationship Context]\n            W --> W1[Foreign Key Details]\n            W --> W2[Relationship Types]\n            W --> W3[Business Flow Context]\n            W --> W4[Linking Columns]\n            \n            W1 & W2 & W3 & W4 --> X[LLM Call: Inter-Table Rules]\n            X --> Y[Cross-Table Validation Rules]\n        end\n        \n        subgraph Inter_Source_Rules [\"Inter-Source Rules\"]\n            Z[Identify Cross-Source Patterns] --> AA[Group Related Sources\\n2-3 sources]\n            AA --> AB[Prepare Cross-Source Context]\n            AB --> AB1[Source Summaries]\n            AB --> AB2[Common Entity Patterns]\n            AB --> AB3[Business Process Flows]\n            \n            AB1 & AB2 & AB3 --> AC[LLM Call: Inter-Source Rules]\n            AC --> AD[Cross-Source Validation Rules]\n        end\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Context_Management_Layer [\"Context Management Layer\"]\n        AE[Global Context Cache]\n        AF[Source Name Mapping]\n        AG[Table ID Mapping]\n        AH[Column ID Mapping]\n        AI[Relationship Cache]\n        \n        C --> AE\n        G --> AI\n        \n        AE -.-> M\n        AE -.-> Q\n        AE -.-> T\n        AE -.-> X\n        AE -.-> AC\n        \n        AF -.-> L3\n        AG -.-> L2\n        AH -.-> L1\n        AI -.-> L4\n        AI -.-> P4\n        AI -.-> W\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Output_Processing [\"Output Processing\"]\n        N & R & U & Y & AD --> AJ[Rule Aggregation]\n        AJ --> AK[Deduplication]\n        AK --> AL[Format Standardization]\n        AL --> AM[MongoDB Storage]\n    end\n    \n    style A fill:#e1f5fe\n    style H fill:#fff3e0\n    style V fill:#f3e5f5\n    style Z fill:#e8f5e9\n    style AE fill:#fff9c4\n    style AJ fill:#ffebee\n```\n\n","x":-288,"y":-66,"width":7048,"height":1786},
		{"id":"6ea6139e95f06b4b","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph \"Initial Setup\"\n        A[MongoDB Collections] --> B[Load Metadata]\n        B --> C[Source Metadata]\n        B --> D[Table Metadata]\n        B --> E[Column Metadata]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Context Building\"\n        C & D & E --> F[Build Universal Context]\n        F --> F1[\"Source Name: source.data.label<br/>Source ID: source.data.id<br/>Source Description<br/>Table Inventory<br/>Embedding Input\"]\n        \n        D --> G[Build Relationship Map]\n        G --> G1[\"Foreign Keys<br/>Primary Keys<br/>Linking Columns<br/>Relationship Types<br/>Relation Descriptions\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Column Level LLM Calls\"\n        H[Column Batch 1-15] --> I{Prepare Prompt}\n        \n        I --> J[System Prompt]\n        I --> K[External Context]\n        I --> L[User Prompt]\n        \n        L --> L1[\"Source: {source.data.label}<br/>Table: {parent_name}<br/>Columns: {be_name, data_type, nullable}<br/>Sample Values: {sample_values[]}<br/>Parent IDs: {parent_id}\"]\n        \n        K --> K1[\"Azure/MongoDB Context<br/>+ Universal Context<br/>+ Relationship Context\"]\n        \n        J & K1 & L1 --> M[LLM Call]\n        M --> N[\"Output Format:<br/>scope_level: 'column'<br/>source.table.column format<br/>SQL queries<br/>Business rules\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Table Level LLM Calls\"\n        O[Single Table] --> P{Prepare Prompt}\n        \n        P --> Q[System Prompt]\n        P --> R[External Context]\n        P --> S[User Prompt]\n        \n        S --> S1[\"Source: {source.data.label}<br/>Table: {table.data.be_name}<br/>Columns List: {columns[]}<br/>Primary Keys: {primary_keys[]}<br/>Foreign Keys: {complete FK objects}<br/>Referenced By: {pk_referencing_tables[]}\"]\n        \n        R --> R1[\"Azure/MongoDB Context<br/>+ Universal Context<br/>+ All Table Relationships\"]\n        \n        Q & R1 & S1 --> T[LLM Call]\n        T --> U[\"Output Format:<br/>scope_level: 'table'<br/>Cross-column validations<br/>Business logic rules\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Source Level LLM Calls\"\n        V[Single Source] --> W{Prepare Prompt}\n        \n        W --> X[System Prompt]\n        W --> Y[External Context]\n        W --> Z[User Prompt]\n        \n        Z --> Z1[\"Source: {source.data.label}<br/>All Tables: {tables[]}<br/>Table Count: {len(tables)}<br/>Aggregated Relationships<br/>Business Context: {embedding_input}\"]\n        \n        Y --> Y1[\"Azure/MongoDB Context<br/>+ Complete Relationship Graph<br/>+ Inter-table Patterns\"]\n        \n        X & Y1 & Z1 --> AA[LLM Call]\n        AA --> AB[\"Output Format:<br/>scope_level: 'source'<br/>Cross-table integrity<br/>Source-wide rules\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Inter-Table LLM Calls\"\n        AC[Related Table Group] --> AD{Prepare Prompt}\n        \n        AD --> AE[System Prompt]\n        AD --> AF[External Context]\n        AD --> AG[User Prompt]\n        \n        AG --> AG1[\"Tables: {3-5 related tables}<br/>FK Relationships: {all FKs between them}<br/>Linking Columns: {detailed}<br/>Relationship Types: {1:1, 1:N, N:N}<br/>Business Flow: {from embedding_inputs}\"]\n        \n        AF --> AF1[\"Universal Context<br/>+ Complete FK Details<br/>+ Business Process Context\"]\n        \n        AE & AF1 & AG1 --> AH[LLM Call]\n        AH --> AI[\"Output Format:<br/>scope_level: 'inter_table'<br/>Referential integrity<br/>Cascade validations<br/>Workflow rules\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Critical Context Elements\"\n        AJ[\"🔑 Always Include\"]\n        AJ --> AK[\"source.data.label (for source.table.column format)\"]\n        AJ --> AL[\"parent_name (table name)\"]\n        AJ --> AM[\"be_name (actual DB names)\"]\n        AJ --> AN[\"Relationship context\"]\n        AJ --> AO[\"embedding_input (business context)\"]\n    end\n    \n    style A fill:#e3f2fd\n    style F fill:#fff9c4\n    style G fill:#f3e5f5\n    style M fill:#c8e6c9\n    style T fill:#c8e6c9\n    style AA fill:#c8e6c9\n    style AH fill:#c8e6c9\n    style AJ fill:#ffcdd2\n```\n","x":2681,"y":4198,"width":2759,"height":5442},
		{"id":"ef0b8bfed0a4443c","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph \"Current Problem\"\n        A[Column Batch Processing] --> B[Missing Source Name]\n        B --> C[\"LLM outputs: table.column<br/>Instead of: source.table.column\"]\n        C --> D[❌ Incorrect Format]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Root Cause\"\n        E[Column Metadata] --> F[\"Has: parent_name (table)<br/>Has: parent_id (table_id)<br/>Missing: source_name ❌\"]\n        F --> G[LLM Cannot Construct Full Path]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Solution Design\"\n        H[Process Source] --> I[Extract source.data.label]\n        I --> J[Pass to All Child Processes]\n        \n        J --> K[Table Processing]\n        J --> L[Column Batch Processing]\n        \n        L --> M[Enhanced Column Context]\n        M --> M1[\"source_name: {source.data.label} ✓<br/>source_id: {source.data.id} ✓<br/>table_name: {parent_name} ✓<br/>column_details: {...} ✓\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Implementation Strategy\"\n        N[Modify _process_column_batch] --> O[Accept source parameter]\n        O --> P[Extract source.data.label]\n        P --> Q[Include in User Prompt]\n        \n        Q --> R[\"Prompt Structure:<br/>Source: {source_name}<br/>Table: {table_name}<br/>Columns: {details}\"]\n        \n        R --> S[LLM Receives Full Context]\n        S --> T[\"✓ Outputs: source.table.column\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Enhanced Prompt Template\"\n        U[\"Column Batch Prompt\"] --> V[\"MANDATORY CONTEXT:<br/>Source Name: General_Ledger<br/>Source ID: 12345<br/>Processing columns for table: journal_entries<br/><br/>Column 1: account_id (varchar, not null)<br/>Column 2: amount (decimal, nullable)<br/>...\"]\n        \n        V --> W[\"Expected Output Format:<br/>data_quality_rule: 'General_Ledger.journal_entries.account_id must not be null'\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Validation Check\"\n        X[Parse LLM Response] --> Y{Contains source.table.column?}\n        Y -->|Yes| Z[✓ Store Rule]\n        Y -->|No| AA[Log Warning & Retry]\n        AA --> AB[Include Example in Retry Prompt]\n    end\n    \n    style D fill:#ffcdd2\n    style F fill:#ffcdd2\n    style T fill:#c8e6c9\n    style Z fill:#c8e6c9\n    style M1 fill:#fff9c4\n```\n","x":3180,"y":10263,"width":2800,"height":1097},
		{"id":"ef6fb9502a3b2026","type":"text","text":"\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Client as Client Trigger\n    participant Main as Main Controller\n    participant DB as MongoDB\n    participant GC as Global Context Builder\n    participant Cache as Context Cache\n    participant P1 as Instance 1 (Source 2)\n    participant P2 as Instance 2 (Source 3)\n    participant LLM as LLM Service\n    participant Dedup as Deduplication\n    participant Store as Rule Storage\n    \n    Note over Client,Store: Day 2: Source 1 already processed. Now processing Sources 2 & 3 in parallel\n    \n    Client->>Main: Process([source_2_id, source_3_id])\n    activate Main\n    \n    %% Check what's already processed\n    Main->>DB: check_processing_status([source_1, source_2, source_3])\n    DB-->>Main: source_1: completed, source_2: not_processed, source_3: not_processed\n    \n    %% Load Global Context - ONCE for all instances\n    Main->>GC: load_global_client_context(client_id)\n    activate GC\n    \n    GC->>DB: get_all_sources_for_client()\n    DB-->>GC: [Source_1_CRM, Source_2_Orders, Source_3_Billing, Source_4_Inventory]\n    \n    GC->>DB: get_all_tables_for_client()\n    DB-->>GC: All tables across all sources\n    \n    GC->>DB: get_all_columns_for_client()\n    DB-->>GC: All columns across all tables\n    \n    GC->>DB: get_existing_rules(source_1)\n    DB-->>GC: Source 1 rules (for reference)\n    \n    Note over GC: Build comprehensive context\n    \n    GC->>GC: build_relationship_map()\n    Note right of GC: Maps:\\n- S2.orders.customer_id → S1.customers.id\\n- S3.invoices.order_id → S2.orders.id\\n- S3.payments.customer_id → S1.customers.id\n    \n    GC->>GC: identify_cross_source_patterns()\n    Note right of GC: Patterns:\\n- customer_id in S1, S2, S3\\n- order_id in S2, S3\\n- invoice_id in S2, S3\n    \n    GC->>GC: extract_business_entities()\n    Note right of GC: Entities:\\n- Customer (S1→S2→S3)\\n- Order (S2→S3)\\n- Payment (S3)\n    \n    GC->>Cache: store_global_context()\n    Cache-->>GC: context_id: ctx_123\n    \n    GC-->>Main: global_context_ready(ctx_123)\n    deactivate GC\n    \n    %% Spawn parallel processors\n    Main->>Main: create_execution_id(exec_abc)\n    \n    par Process Source 2\n        Main->>P1: process_source(source_2_id, ctx_123, exec_abc)\n        activate P1\n        \n        P1->>Cache: get_global_context(ctx_123)\n        Cache-->>P1: Full global context\n        \n        P1->>DB: get_source_metadata(source_2)\n        DB-->>P1: Source_2_Orders metadata\n        \n        P1->>DB: get_tables_for_source(source_2)\n        DB-->>P1: [orders, order_lines, order_status]\n        \n        %% Process first table: orders\n        P1->>DB: get_columns_for_table(orders)\n        DB-->>P1: 30 columns\n        \n        P1->>P1: create_batches(30 columns)\n        Note right of P1: Batch 1: cols 1-15, Batch 2: cols 16-30\n        \n        rect rgb(200, 230, 255)\n            P1->>P1: prepare_batch_context(batch_1)\n            Note right of P1: Context includes:\\n- Source_2 be_name: \"Orders_DB\"\\n- Table be_name: \"orders\"\\n- Columns 1-15 details\\n- ALL sources summary\\n- Relationships to S1, S3\\n- Patterns across sources\n            \n            P1->>LLM: generate_rules(batch_1_context)\n            Note right of LLM: Prompt includes:\\n\"You are processing Orders_DB.orders\\nGlobal context shows:\\n- CRM_DB.customers exists\\n- Billing_DB.invoices exists\\nGenerate rules for all scopes\"\n            \n            LLM-->>P1: Rules for batch_1\n            Note left of LLM: Returns:\\n- 30 column rules\\n- 3 table rules\\n- 2 cross_table rules\\n- 4 cross_source rules (including Orders→CRM)\n        end\n        \n        %% Continue with remaining batches\n        P1->>LLM: generate_rules(batch_2_context)\n        LLM-->>P1: Rules for batch_2\n        \n        P1->>LLM: generate_rules(table_group_context)\n        LLM-->>P1: Source-level rules\n        \n        P1->>Store: store_temp_rules(source_2_rules, exec_abc)\n        Store-->>P1: stored\n        \n        deactivate P1\n    \n    and Process Source 3\n        Main->>P2: process_source(source_3_id, ctx_123, exec_abc)\n        activate P2\n        \n        P2->>Cache: get_global_context(ctx_123)\n        Cache-->>P2: Same global context as P1\n        \n        P2->>DB: get_source_metadata(source_3)\n        DB-->>P2: Source_3_Billing metadata\n        \n        P2->>DB: get_tables_for_source(source_3)\n        DB-->>P2: [invoices, payments, refunds]\n        \n        %% Process invoices table\n        P2->>DB: get_columns_for_table(invoices)\n        DB-->>P2: 25 columns\n        \n        P2->>P2: create_batches(25 columns)\n        Note right of P2: Batch 1: cols 1-15, Batch 2: cols 16-25\n        \n        rect rgb(255, 200, 230)\n            P2->>P2: prepare_batch_context(batch_1)\n            Note right of P2: Context includes:\\n- Source_3 be_name: \"Billing_DB\"\\n- Table be_name: \"invoices\"\\n- Columns 1-15 details\\n- SAME global context as P1\\n- Sees Orders_DB exists\\n- Sees CRM_DB exists\n            \n            P2->>LLM: generate_rules(batch_1_context)\n            Note right of LLM: Can generate:\\n- Billing→Orders rules\\n- Billing→CRM rules\\nEven though processing S3\n            \n            LLM-->>P2: Rules for batch_1\n            Note left of LLM: Returns:\\n- 30 column rules\\n- 3 table rules\\n- 2 cross_table rules\\n- 5 cross_source rules (including Billing→Orders, Billing→CRM)\n        end\n        \n        P2->>LLM: generate_rules(remaining_batches)\n        LLM-->>P2: More rules\n        \n        P2->>Store: store_temp_rules(source_3_rules, exec_abc)\n        Store-->>P2: stored\n        \n        deactivate P2\n    end\n    \n    %% Post-processing phase\n    Main->>Dedup: deduplicate_rules(exec_abc)\n    activate Dedup\n    \n    Dedup->>Store: get_temp_rules(exec_abc)\n    Store-->>Dedup: Rules from P1 and P2\n    \n    Note over Dedup: Potential duplicates:\\nP1: Orders.customer_id → CRM.customers.id\\nP2: Billing.customer_id → CRM.customers.id\\nP1: Orders.order_id → Billing.invoices.order_id\\nP2: Billing.invoices.order_id → Orders.order_id\n    \n    Dedup->>Dedup: identify_duplicates()\n    Dedup->>Dedup: merge_bidirectional_rules()\n    Dedup->>Dedup: resolve_conflicts()\n    \n    Dedup->>Store: store_final_rules()\n    Store-->>Dedup: Success\n    \n    Dedup->>DB: update_processing_log([source_2, source_3])\n    DB-->>Dedup: Updated\n    \n    deactivate Dedup\n    \n    Main->>Store: get_generation_summary(exec_abc)\n    Store-->>Main: Summary stats\n    \n    Main-->>Client: Success: Generated rules for S2, S3 (including cross-source with S1)\n    deactivate Main\n    \n    Note over Client,Store: Key Points:\\n1. Global context loaded ONCE\\n2. Both instances see ALL sources\\n3. Can generate cross-source rules to Source 1\\n4. Deduplication handles overlaps\n```\n\n","x":7200,"y":-11040,"width":7640,"height":4620}
	],
	"edges":[]
}